    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining our lineup. His elite sprint speed and aggressive matchup against Kodai Senga make him our highest-scoring play; despite a minor park penalty, his strong platoon advantage and leadoff spot solidify his floor. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) also provides immense value against Brady Singer, bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a robust platoon edge that drives his efficiency well above the baseline. Further down the order, **Caleb Durbin** (69.66) and **Junior Caminero** (68.95) are strong starts; **Caleb Durbin** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a soft matchup against Ryan Feltner, while **Junior Caminero** is positioned to capitalize on Michael Wacha\u2019s elevated expected ERA.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge** (47.21), who narrowly missed the cut for our active lineup. While his leadoff position is typically a multiplier for success, his unfavorable platoon matchup against Shota Imanaga ultimately depressed his score, leaving him on the bench in favor of hitters with higher efficiency ceilings like **Nelson Velazquez** (55.77). We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Dillon Dingler** (48.65), whose score is suppressed by a challenging draw against Gerrit Cole; should his projected #2 spot in the order be shifted, we may revisit his utility. Additionally, we are exercising caution with **Yordan Alvarez** (58.52), whose world-class xwOBA of 0.447 is currently being dampened by the elite 3.15 xERA of Dylan Cease. With **Rece Hinds** and **Hyeseong Kim** currently assigned to the minors, the organization remains focused on maintaining efficiency with the active roster to preserve our game caps.",
